-- title:
--   Join of two module-finite K-spanning orders
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $K$ a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and $A$ a commutative ring carrying both a $K$-Hopf algebra structure and an $R$-algebra structure, the two being compatible in the sense that $R \to K \to A$ is a scalar tower. Let $S$ and $S'$ be $R$-subalgebras of $A$, each finitely generated as an $R$-module, and assume that $S$ spans $A$ over $K$, i.e. the $K$-submodule of $A$ generated by the underlying set of $S$ is all of $A$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the join $S \sqcup S'$ in the lattice of $R$-subalgebras of $A$ (the $R$-subalgebra generated by $S \cup S'$): first, $S \sqcup S'$ is again finitely generated as an $R$-module; second, the $K$-submodule of $A$ spanned by the underlying set of $S \sqcup S'$ is all of $A$. No Hopf-theoretic condition (comultiplication, antipode or counit stability) is imposed on $S$ or $S'$.
--
--   This is the stability of the two "order" conditions — module-finiteness over $R$ and generation of $A$ over $K$ — under passage to the join of two $R$-subalgebras, the step which allows the set of Hopf orders in a $K$-Hopf algebra $A$ to be manipulated as a lattice. It is used in the construction of a greatest Hopf order ([`HopfOrder.exists_isGreatest`](thm.html#HopfOrder.exists_isGreatest)) and in the base-change statement [`HopfAlgebra.existsUnique_bialgHom_baseChange_eq_of_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.existsUnique_bialgHom_baseChange_eq_of_pow_eq_one).
